35,2,1,talk,Rin,,"Wow, the pilot floor takes almost ten minutes just to start working! And those unplanned shuffles sound like a total nightmare. We really can't have things being that messy or slow!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"The costs are quite rigid. We are billed by area regardless of occupancy, and every single desk move incurs a specific fee. Frequent changes to the layout will be a recurring financial drain.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Mizuki,,"It seems we have a conflict between fairness and productivity. The staff survey shows a strong desire for daylight, yet the current plan leaves some people in the dark. Also, overhearing others is vital for new joiners.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Shion,,"The environment is far from uniform. There's a significant noise difference between the corridor and the windows, and more importantly, our equipment takes days of fine-tuning to actually be comfortable. Constant movement would be a disaster.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"I found out that we all arrive at such different times! If we do something first-come, first-served, it's not really fair. But sitting near each other really helps us communicate and skip the boring notes!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Rin,,"If we move around too much, we'll just waste time and be surrounded by boxes for weeks! We need something that doesn't make every morning a chore or every change a disaster.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"Given the costs, a layout that requires frequent adjustments is unsustainable. We are paying for the space regardless of how we use it, but we pay extra every time we move a desk.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Mizuki,,"If we prioritize the joiners' experience, we need a layout that encourages organic communication. However, we must also address the daylight issue so that a few people aren't stuck in the dark.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Shion,,"If we prioritize ergonomics and noise levels, we cannot ignore that our gear requires stability. Moving seats frequently would mean spending days in physical discomfort just to settle back in.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"That's so true! If we want to keep that great communication and help new people learn, we should be careful about how we split us up. We need a plan that keeps us connected!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Rin,,"I'm worried that if we pick something where we move all the time, we'll just be wasting our gaps! We need a plan that's quick and doesn't cause a huge mess.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,Financial stability and operational efficiency suggest we avoid any option that triggers repeated facilities charges or creates daily time losses. A permanent or infrequent arrangement is the only logical choice.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Mizuki,,"We must also consider that a first-come, first-served system would unfairly penalize those who arrive later, while a fixed plan might leave some permanently without window access. We need a balanced solution.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Shion,,"The data is clear. Between the noise disparity and the time required to calibrate our workstations, any system involving frequent movement is illogical. We cannot sacrifice physical health and focus for the sake of variety.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Yumi,,"I agree with Shion! If we move too much, we lose that special connection and the ease of just asking a question across the desk. Let's find a way to stay close and comfortable!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Rin,,I just want us to be fast and happy! No more long setups or weeks of boxes. Let's pick the option that keeps our mornings simple and our desks steady!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,We must prioritize a layout that minimizes both financial waste and time loss. Any option involving frequent shifts or daily reconfiguration is an inefficient use of our limited budget and working hours.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Mizuki,,"We need a system that ensures no one is permanently disadvantaged by the layout, while still supporting the organic learning and communication that our new joiners found so valuable. Fairness must be a core part of our decision.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Shion,,"Stability is the only logical priority. If we ignore the noise levels and the time it takes to adjust our equipment, we are choosing inefficiency and physical strain. We need a layout that remains constant.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Yumi,,I totally agree! We need a plan that lets us stay connected and comfortable without making things unfair for the people who arrive later. Let's pick something that keeps us together!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
