67,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"It is rare for a team to reach a consensus so quickly, but the data makes the conclusion inevitable. Option C minimizes waste and maximizes stability. I maintain my vote for Option C.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Mizuki,,"It is a relief that we can all agree. By choosing Option C, we can now focus on how to assign those seats fairly, ensuring everyone's needs are met. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shion,,"The logic is undeniable. When you factor in the noise, the ergonomics, and the cost, any other choice is simply irrational. I stand by my vote for Option C.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Yumi,,I'm just so happy we're all on the same page! It's the best way to keep us all connected and happy. I definitely vote for Option C!,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"Since the consensus is absolute and the reasoning is sound, there is no need for further deliberation. I vote for Option C.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
